{"ts": "2026-11-21T00:06:21.615194Z", "run_id": "r-20261120T2324Z-a10b", "unit": "openspec:add-run-inputs-form", "seq": 66, "type": "task.done", "task": "3.3", "base": "9296a3e10562a31b682f5c8cf6fbeb32d4a3d389", "parents": [], "notes": "The browser test's dry-run refusal mock answers 422 with code INVALID_REQUEST, which `dryRunFormErrors` turns into a `$form` message. DryRunPanel therefore derives the rows to open and their notes from `details.fields` entries whose `field` starts with `body/fakes/<node>`, whatever the code. It also opens a row when the Fakes error contains `<node>: `. I could not run the e2e tests here, so the row-opening behaviour is unverified in a browser.", "suppressions": []}
